  "usage": "Give modes as rows {item, mode, effect, cause, s, o, d (whole numbers 1-10), action, and optionally rs, ro, rd: the scores after the action, blank = unchanged}, method = rpn | so, the action threshold (rpnMin for rpn, soMin for so) and sevMin. It returns the modes in risk order with score, share of the total and whether action is needed and why, counts of modes needing action and those without a plan, the Pareto count holding 80 % of the risk, a bar chart, an action list text, the risk after actions when revised scores are given, and result.fmea with every mode's scores, share and status as data. Use it to prioritise design or process risks on a small project; it is not a full AIAG-VDA Action Priority analysis.",
  "sources": [
    "AIAG Potential Failure Mode and Effects Analysis, 4th edition (2008): S/O/D 1-10 scales and RPN",
    "IEC 60812:2018 Failure modes and effects analysis (FMEA and FMECA), RPN and criticality",
    "AIAG & VDA FMEA Handbook (2019) - notes the move to Action Priority; severity 9-10 = safety / regulatory",
    "Rule of thumb: RPN action threshold 100"
  ],
  "layout": "custom"
